nd{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "162a4f62-2177-5623-998d-5746dbddde07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 6-(-7)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{5}{9}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{5}{9}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250989 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250989 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250989 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "34813407-d25e-5329-a49d-90dd01f166fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251576 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251576 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251576 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7b123f7b-16ce-5745-8c7f-29a3af037f52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251604 #edb/ref 1080 "2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251604 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251604 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7da8a500-b479-5c6c-814e-26884a69c42f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251761 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251761 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251761 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8e807c03-b5d6-572a-8190-75f1c2889bc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252488 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252488 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252488 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dc04463b-6bd3-537d-b8a6-0f5c1de23fda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186250989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186251761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252946 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "516c4e1a-8e61-51a8-bdbd-a5bccc229947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253323 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186252946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253323 #edb/ref 1069 "q-117278" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253323 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253323 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{′}(1)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253323 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c2ae5d5-ee50-5ac5-adef-e81c842f8f25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253323 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{a}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $-{x}^{3}$ and $x.$\n\nThe integrand ${t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t)+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-(-3{x}^{2}){u}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{(-{x}^{3})}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{x}^{3})+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{x}^{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=-{x}^{3}.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(1).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{1}^{3}+{1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡1 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡1 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256876 #edb/ref 1080 "x{2}^{x}=x+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2){x}^{2}+\\frac{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)^{2}{x}^{3}}{2}+⋯" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256876 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256876 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a4a297e-b4a6-5cad-93c5-88029bba263f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257324 #edb/ref 1080 "x{2}^{x}=1+x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+⋯" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257324 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257324 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3c9116be-92bf-51fe-a69a-fd4ba85e6916" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257351 #edb/ref 1080 "x{2}^{x}=1+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)x+\\frac{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)^{2}{x}^{2}}{2}+⋯" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257351 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257351 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f57ea8d-f142-5079-b581-f6ee26810a1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257503 #edb/ref 1080 "x{2}^{x}=x+{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+⋯" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257503 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257503 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "54698d2b-89af-5198-a42a-49279c3ffa2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258353 #edb/ref 1080 "x{2}^{x}=x+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2){x}^{2}+\\frac{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)^{2}{x}^{3}}{6}+⋯" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258353 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258353 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b50a01e8-84ad-57b9-832f-8c540f2b388f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259132 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186256876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259132 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257324 #edb/re