n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}t+u \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}t+2{u}^{′}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}({u}^{″}t+2{u}^{′})+2t({u}^{′}t+u)-2ut & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}{t}^{3}+2{u}^{′}{t}^{2}+2{u}^{′}{t}^{2}+2ut-2ut & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}{t}^{3}+4{u}^{′}{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}({u}^{″}t+4{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}t+4{u}^{′}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}t+4w=0.\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n\n$$\nw=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{{t}^{4}}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{{t}^{4}}\\,⟹\\,u=-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{3{t}^{3}}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(t)=ut$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(t)=(-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{3{t}^{3}}+{c}_{2})t.\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=-3$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}\\cdot t=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=At+\\frac{B}{{t}^{2}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266433 #edb/ref 1080 "8.1%" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266433 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266433 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "209a5dc2-51b8-5cf8-a3fd-432567049203" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266453 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266453 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266453 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "228b048a-6de3-56b6-a3e7-0871c1de3843" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266456 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266456 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266456 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "22995146-b5cd-