417] [17592186268415 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268415 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268415 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268415 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268415 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268415 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268415 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186266502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268415 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0642bb25-91a1-5589-b640-3a5b72872474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186267145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268645 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8681df6c-6663-5b99-800e-3e89e88d4c91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269176 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269176 #edb/ref 1069 "q-138132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269176 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269176 #edb/ref 1071 "The maximum value of the quadratic form $Q(x)=-2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2},$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to $2.$ Which of the following is a vector $x$ at which the maximum is attained?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269176 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cc5eba78-8576-573c-99ab-7374b3ba103b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269176 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-2I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269411 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269411 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269411 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10032c13-43f8-533c-aae8-cdbe8ef3937a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269831 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269831 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269831 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3dc653f0-653a-51c8-9dde-134e1ea1131e"